    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0H1SUM4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 0's partial sum (chain 4 of 13), Y = A0 XOR B0; the duplicated chains carry the partial sum onto the operand pins of the second half adder — one waveguide per pin, so the textbook shared stage is instantiated once per consumer; this chain feeds T0H2N5.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_e78727b4d7e94d658f435518f4e13dfb",
        "IdGuid": "b627105c-2410-4de1-942a-7046bf675390",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "3c390942-cb80-4d55-b0e6-63e97983f0bc",
          "f7e98046-f8de-498a-8fe0-4c78e79c3335",
