    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0H1SUM13",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: sum stage of stage 0's partial sum (chain 13 of 13), Y = A0 XOR B0; this extra chain feeds the duplicated carry stage T0H2N5C10.B — one waveguide per pin. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_214fe36750184727a08b44c5c25bfab2",
        "IdGuid": "4b6a77f5-9e05-49de-8cb2-f51727ef50d0",
