    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1OROUT",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 1, Y = NAND(NOT(C1), NOT(C2)) = C1 OR C2 = majority(A1, B1, C1) — copy 1 of 7: the ripple carry C2 fans out onto stage 2's 7 carry-in pins, one waveguide per pin, so the whole carry-OR subtree is duplicated per consumer; this copy feeds T2H2N1A.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_e2cf63a5920d4c54bfef5d350442a5dd",
        "IdGuid": "a9bbecdd-1e2c-4e4b-97f8-0b9ca875ed98",
